": "On {December 31, 1857|December thirty-first, eighteen fifty-seven}, London's letter arrived. The Queen's choice: Ottawa.", "cam": [{"from": "prev", "t": 0}, {"fit": [-77.3, 44.0, -74.2, 46.1], "pad": 0.02, "t": 2.2, "ease": "power3.inOut"}, {"fit": [-77.3, 44.0, -74.2, 46.1], "pad": -0.03, "t": "end", "ease": "sine.inOut"}], "data": {"layers": {}, "labels": [{"text": "Ottawa", "at": [-75.7, 45.42], "style": "big", "cue": "ottawa"}, {"text": "Dec. 31, 1857", "at": [-75.7, 44.55], "style": "tag", "anchor": "c", "cue": "december"}], "source": "City of Ottawa; PSPC, History of Parliament Hill"}, "pin": {"expr": "surprised", "acts": [{"t": 0.3, "look": [8, -6]}, {"cue": "ottawa", "hop": true, "expr": "proud"}]}}, {"type": "map", "chapter": "Why Ottawa", "narration": "Why there? First, it sat right on the line between Canada West and Canada East.", "cam": [{"fit": [-77.3, 44.0, -74.2, 46.1], "pad": 0.02, "t": 0}, {"fit": [-77.3, 44.0, -74.2, 46.1], "pad": -0.03, "t": "end", "ease": "sine.inOut"}], "data": {"layers": {}, "labels": [{"text": "Ottawa", "at": [-75.7, 45.42], "style": "callout", "anchor": "n", "cue": "there"}, {"text": "Canada West", "at": [-76.6, 44.75], "style": "region", "cue": "west"}, {"text": "Canada East", "at": [-74.7, 45.85], "style": "region", "cue": "east"}, {"text": "The line", "at": [-74.9, 45.25], "style": "tag", "anchor": "c", "cue": "line"}], "source": "City of Ottawa, Ottawa Becomes the Capital"}, "pin": {"expr": "thinking", "acts": [{"t": 0.3, "look": [8, -6]}, {"cue": "line", "point": [-74.95, 45.5], "hold": 0.6}]}}, {"type": "map", "narration": "Second, it sat at the mouth of the Rideau Canal, a military route begun in {1826|eighteen twenty-six}, running south to Kingston.", "cam": [{"fit": [-77.3, 44.0, -74.2, 46.1], "pad": 0.02, "t": 0}, {"fit": [-77.3, 44.0, -74.2, 46.1], "pad": -0.03, "t": "end", "ease": "sine.inOut"}], "data": {"layers": {"routes": [{"via": [[-75.7, 45.42], [-76.02, 44.9], [-76.49, 44.23]], "dur": 2.4, "cue": "ride